00:42:35.883 --> 00:42:37.072
&gt;&gt; The Master of Arts and

00:42:37.072 --> 00:42:41.501
Business Research recognizes the
accomplishments of students have completed

00:42:41.501 --> 00:42:45.996
the coursework and fulfilled the research
requirements of the Masters degree,

00:42:45.996 --> 00:42:48.111
and thus have became domain experts,

00:42:48.111 --> 00:42:53.185
but who are not continuing on to do
further work required for the PhD degree.

00:42:53.185 --> 00:42:56.364
Although none of this year's
candidates for the Master of Arts and

00:42:56.364 --> 00:43:00.227
Business Research are present for today's
ceremony, their names are listed in

00:43:00.227 --> 00:43:03.505
the program and we celebrate their
accomplishments nonetheless.

00:43:03.505 --> 00:43:13.505
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE].

00:43:15.013 --> 00:43:18.887
&gt;&gt; This year marks the 43rd class of
students who graduate with Certificate in

00:43:18.887 --> 00:43:21.100
Public Management and Social Innovation.

00:43:22.210 --> 00:43:24.305
Founded by Dean Emeritus, Arjay Miller,

00:43:24.305 --> 00:43:28.330
the certificate program educates leaders
for social and environmental change.

00:43:29.550 --> 00:43:34.359
Today's graduates really do embody
the spirit of our motto, change lives,

00:43:34.359 --> 00:43:37.910
change organizations, change the world.

00:43:37.910 --> 00:43:40.390
These students have already
shown their commitment,

00:43:40.390 --> 00:43:43.158
using management skills to
alleviate global social problems.

00:43:43.158 --> 00:43:49.110
For example, they participated in a wide
range of social innovation courses,

00:43:49.110 --> 00:43:53.510
covering topics such as healthcare
innovation, education reform,

00:43:53.510 --> 00:43:57.480
business at the bottom of the pyramid,
and sustainable energy markets.

00:43:58.510 --> 00:44:00.700
They explored roles with
high social impact,

00:44:00.700 --> 00:44:05.480
such as board governance,
impact investing, and philanthropy.

00:44:05.480 --> 00:44:10.670
They traveled on social innovation trips
to places like Bangladesh, Bhutan,

00:44:10.670 --> 00:44:14.300
Brazil, China, Kenya and
Rwanda, to see for

00:44:14.300 --> 00:44:18.400
themselves what is possible to
address issues of extreme poverty,

00:44:18.400 --> 00:44:23.070
access to healthcare, education,
sustainability and more.

00:44:23.070 --> 00:44:26.970
And finally, some of them have developed
their own social enterprise and

00:44:26.970 --> 00:44:28.930
are ready to launch
right after graduation.

00:44:30.250 --> 00:44:33.910
I am proud to tell you that this year we

00:44:33.910 --> 00:44:39.310
have 118 recipients of the Certificate in
Public Management and Social Innovation.

00:44:39.310 --> 00:44:41.410
Their names are listed in
the commencement program.

00:44:42.590 --> 00:44:46.899
I now ask those 118 students to stand and
be recognized for

00:44:46.899 --> 00:44:51.548
completing a formal course of
study in the management of public,

00:44:51.548 --> 00:44:54.690
nonprofit, social issue organizations.

00:44:55.950 --> 00:44:56.646
Congratulations.

00:44:56.646 --> 00:45:06.646
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

00:45:12.781 --> 00:45:15.890
&gt;&gt; Good afternoon,
on this festive and beautiful day.

00:45:17.040 --> 00:45:21.490
It is my pleasure as Director of
the Stanford MSX program, to present

00:45:21.490 --> 00:45:25.672
this years graduates, who will receive the
degree of Master of Science in Management.

00:45:26.720 --> 00:45:31.140
The mission of the MSX program is to
provide experienced leaders, men and

00:45:31.140 --> 00:45:34.030
women, who have spent at least
eight years in professional and

00:45:34.030 --> 00:45:37.100
management roles,
the opportunity to prepare themselves for

00:45:37.100 --> 00:45:40.260
increasingly senior positions
in organizations they will lead.

00:45:41.460 --> 00:45:43.141
The program is a full-time,

00:45:43.141 --> 00:45:48.180
year-long course of academic study, giving
these students an all too rare chance for

00:45:48.180 --> 00:45:51.650
reflection and growth in the midst
of an already accomplished career.

00:45:52.950 --> 00:45:56.880
Simultaneously, they bring to the GSB
a perspective shaped by experience with

00:45:56.880 --> 00:45:59.500
difficult organizational challenges,

00:45:59.500 --> 00:46:02.620
enriching our academic
community as a result.

00:46:02.620 --> 00:46:06.280
While studying at Stanford, these students
carry the title of Sloan Fellows,

00:46:06.280 --> 00:46:09.714
a tradition that dates to the year
the program was founded in 1957.

00:46:11.030 --> 00:46:15.270
This year's Fellows came to Stanford
from across the United States and

00:46:15.270 --> 00:46:17.020
22 additional countries.

00:46:17.020 --> 00:46:19.750
Many Fellows are sponsored
by their employers.

00:46:19.750 --> 00:46:20.990
Others will be joining, or

00:46:20.990 --> 00:46:24.120
creating innovative new
enterprises after graduation.

00:46:25.270 --> 00:46:29.110
Having completed all the academic
requirements of the program, this year's

00:46:29.110 --> 00:46:33.670
89 Sloan Fellows will join the worldwide
family of Stanford Business School alumni.

00:46:35.260 --> 00:46:37.440
On behalf of the administration
of the program,

00:46:37.440 --> 00:46:41.400
and the faculty who have taught them,
join me in wishing

00:46:41.400 --> 00:46:44.828
each of them great fulfillment and success
in the next phase of their careers.

00:46:44.828 --> 00:46:54.828
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

