01:01:35.615 --> 01:01:36.245
&gt;&gt; All right, calm down.

01:01:36.245 --> 01:01:37.920
You haven't graduated yet, okay?

01:01:37.920 --> 01:01:42.505
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; Distinguished guests, faculty, staff,

01:01:42.505 --> 01:01:44.240
families and friends.

01:01:44.240 --> 01:01:47.270
&gt;&gt; The MBA students gathered
here before us today,

01:01:47.270 --> 01:01:51.610
achieved great distinction 2 years ago
when they successfully navigated our

01:01:51.610 --> 01:01:53.385
extremely competitive admissions process.

01:01:53.385 --> 01:01:57.700
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Since then,

01:01:57.700 --> 01:02:04.599
they have acquired solid foundations

01:02:04.599 --> 01:02:09.142
in general management.

01:02:09.142 --> 01:02:15.270
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
[APPLAUSE]

01:02:15.270 --> 01:02:16.750
&gt;&gt; And have pursued deeper study

01:02:16.750 --> 01:02:17.859
in their areas of interest.

01:02:19.440 --> 01:02:21.340
They have engaged in personal growth and

01:02:21.340 --> 01:02:23.370
built relationships that
will last a lifetime.

01:02:23.370 --> 01:02:28.820
They have helped the school and the
community in many extremely valuable ways.

01:02:28.820 --> 01:02:30.810
They are an impressive group,
and are ready and

01:02:30.810 --> 01:02:34.370
worthy to join the ranks
of our illustrious alumni.

01:02:34.370 --> 01:02:37.060
Therefore, ladies and gentlemen,
it's my great honor and

01:02:37.060 --> 01:02:41.787
privilege to present to you
the Stanford MBA class of

01:02:41.787 --> 01:02:49.799
2015.

01:02:49.799 --> 01:02:59.799
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:03:07.645 --> 01:03:12.238
&gt;&gt; You're the 90th MBA graduating class at
the Stanford Graduate School of Business

01:03:12.238 --> 01:03:15.185
and in my somewhat biased opinion,
the best one yet.

01:03:15.185 --> 01:03:20.950
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; As

01:03:20.950 --> 01:03:24.590
you leave the lead lives of impact and
meaning, I fully expect back your

01:03:24.590 --> 01:03:29.250
accomplishments at Stanford will pale in
comparison to your future achievements.

01:03:29.250 --> 01:03:31.445
But I hope your memories of
the GSP will remain fresh, and

01:03:31.445 --> 01:03:33.196
that you will stay
involved with the school.

01:03:33.196 --> 01:03:37.524
All of them played an important role in
your academic experience ranging from

01:03:37.524 --> 01:03:41.055
serving as judges in the executive
challenge acting as mentors

01:03:41.055 --> 01:03:42.797
in entrepreneurial courses.

01:03:42.797 --> 01:03:47.139
Our alumni also played a key role in
your graduation experience today.

01:03:47.139 --> 01:03:51.070
Three years ago we had made the decision
to do graduation within the air

01:03:51.070 --> 01:03:53.736
conditioned confines of Maples Pavilion,
but

01:03:53.736 --> 01:03:58.066
the class of 2012 protested, came out
strongly in favor of having you all

01:03:58.066 --> 01:04:01.222
have a sweltering graduation
experience here, okay.

01:04:01.222 --> 01:04:05.666
&gt;&gt; [LAUGH]
&gt;&gt; It's my wish that you will engage

01:04:05.666 --> 01:04:09.380
with the GSB's academic mission
as alumni and give your time and

01:04:09.380 --> 01:04:12.760
experience generously to future classes.

01:04:12.760 --> 01:04:17.267
Your class has already demonstrated its
desire to stay connected to the GSB,

01:04:17.267 --> 01:04:19.832
and to support the school
in a meaningful way

01:04:19.832 --> 01:04:23.115
through your participation
in the class gift program.

01:04:23.115 --> 01:04:27.790
I must recognize the extraordinary
result of 98.25% of you

01:04:27.790 --> 01:04:30.172
pledging to give back to the GSB.

01:04:30.172 --> 01:04:39.772
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; For

01:04:39.772 --> 01:04:44.632
the seven students who were not moved
by my half now, half later video,

01:04:44.632 --> 01:04:46.177
we will hunt you down.

01:04:46.177 --> 01:04:55.236
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; So,

01:04:55.236 --> 01:05:00.032
at this time, I would like to ask the
members of the Student Association Senate

01:05:00.032 --> 01:05:03.677
and the members of the seven
SA committees to please stand.

01:05:03.677 --> 01:05:13.677
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:05:14.928 --> 01:05:16.879
&gt;&gt; Keep standing.

01:05:16.879 --> 01:05:21.046
The SA has a profound
impact on the academic,

01:05:21.046 --> 01:05:25.874
extracurricular, and
social lives of students and

01:05:25.874 --> 01:05:33.550
serves as an important conduit between
the students, faculty and staff.

01:05:33.550 --> 01:05:36.188
Serving on the SA is
a tremendous amount of work.

01:05:36.188 --> 01:05:38.690
Most of which happens behind the scenes,
and

01:05:38.690 --> 01:05:41.150
is the foundation for
much of the student experience.

01:05:41.150 --> 01:05:43.321
So please join me again in
a round of applause for

01:05:43.321 --> 01:05:45.288
this committed group of student leaders.

01:05:45.288 --> 01:05:46.054
Thank you.

01:05:46.054 --> 01:05:55.140
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; At

01:05:55.140 --> 01:06:00.218
this time I would like to ask
the Arbuckle Leadership Fellows to stand.

01:06:00.218 --> 01:06:10.218
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:06:13.831 --> 01:06:17.237
&gt;&gt; The Leadership Fellows program plays
an integral role in the GSB Leadership

01:06:17.237 --> 01:06:21.016
curriculum by bringing together a group of
talented second year students to support

01:06:21.016 --> 01:06:24.150
the leadership development
of the first year class.

01:06:24.150 --> 01:06:26.520
On behalf of the school,
I thank these 68 students for

01:06:26.520 --> 01:06:30.265
their tireless work, their extraordinary
dedication to their MBA1 squads and

01:06:30.265 --> 01:06:34.750
coaches, and for inspiring a significant
number of first year students

01:06:34.750 --> 01:06:37.430
to seek out this unique
leadership opportunity.

01:06:37.430 --> 01:06:40.280
They are a role model for
student leadership at its best.

01:06:40.280 --> 01:06:44.689
Please join me in thanking this
remarkable group of students.

01:06:44.689 --> 01:06:52.911
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Finally,

01:06:52.911 --> 01:06:56.644
I would like to ask the student leaders
of the global study trips, the social

01:06:56.644 --> 01:07:00.977
innovation study trips, and the Stanford
Tsinghua exchange program to please stand.

01:07:00.977 --> 01:07:10.977
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

01:07:16.795 --> 01:07:20.885
&gt;&gt; These 102 outstanding student leaders
partnered with the school on a critical

01:07:20.885 --> 01:07:25.150
component of the GSB education,
the global experience requirement.

01:07:25.150 --> 01:07:26.780
They served as peer educators for

01:07:26.780 --> 01:07:31.410
almost 600 students, traveling to
23 countries, helping them discover

01:07:31.410 --> 01:07:36.220
how business skills are relevant in a wide
variety of industries and institutions.

01:07:36.220 --> 01:07:40.760
As the GSB show made clear, they succeeded
in driving home an important lesson,

01:07:40.760 --> 01:07:42.909
different countries are different.

01:07:42.909 --> 01:07:50.279
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; For

01:07:50.279 --> 01:07:51.938
acting as ambassadors to the GSB and for

01:07:51.938 --> 01:07:54.760
their indelible impact on
the students they led, we thank them.

01:07:54.760 --> 01:08:00.580
Please join me in a round of applause for
this exceptional group of students.

01:08:00.580 --> 01:08:07.307
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; In the next few

01:08:07.307 --> 01:08:10.709
minutes we will begin reading the names of
the graduates in alphabetical order and

01:08:10.709 --> 01:08:13.790
we'll invite them forward
to receive their diploma.

01:08:13.790 --> 01:08:18.150
Names will be read by Derrick Bolton,
Assistant Dean for MBA Admissions and

01:08:18.150 --> 01:08:21.330
Margaret Hayes, Assistant Dean for
the MBA program.

01:08:21.330 --> 01:08:24.470
Graduates will receive their
diplomas from Dean Saloner.

01:08:25.580 --> 01:08:30.140
So, as Garth mentioned, we have the great
privilege to have Dean Miller here today.

01:08:30.140 --> 01:08:34.211
All of you have undoubtedly heard of Arjay
Miller, and from the great reception he

01:08:34.211 --> 01:08:37.339
got, I presume many of you
are friends of Arjay Miller as well.

01:08:37.339 --> 01:08:45.996
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; Arjay

01:08:45.996 --> 01:08:48.688
served in the US Air Force
during the second World War and

01:08:48.688 --> 01:08:53.370
was later one of the so-called whiz kids
who revolutionized Ford Motor Company.

01:08:53.370 --> 01:08:55.330
Arjay became president of Ford and

01:08:55.330 --> 01:09:00.850
then later the much admired full
Dean of the GSB from 1968 to 1978.

01:09:00.850 --> 01:09:03.470
His sterling leadership of
the school is legendary.

01:09:03.470 --> 01:09:08.096
In honor of Dean Miller's service, the top
10% of the class ranked by academic

01:09:08.096 --> 01:09:11.270
performance are designated
as Arjay Miller Scholars.

01:09:11.270 --> 01:09:14.554
As we read the names of the graduates,
we will also announce if they have

01:09:14.554 --> 01:09:16.984
achieved the distinction
of Arjay Miller Scholar.

01:09:16.984 --> 01:09:19.458
And the award comes with
a special privilege,

01:09:19.458 --> 01:09:23.457
Dean Miller will personally congratulate
the Arjay Miller Scholars after

01:09:23.457 --> 01:09:26.328
they have received their
diploma from Dean Saloner.

01:09:26.328 --> 01:09:30.972
Margaret and Derrick,
would you please begin.

