01:57:37.546 --> 01:57:42.303
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; It now is my pleasure to

01:57:42.303 --> 01:57:48.670
introduce the presentation of awards.

01:57:48.670 --> 01:57:50.900
Susan Arbuckle will present
the Arbuckle award,

01:57:50.900 --> 01:57:55.120
followed by Madavrajan who will present
the RubercheckAward and the Ford Scholar.

01:57:55.120 --> 01:57:55.965
Susan.

01:57:55.965 --> 01:58:05.760
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]
&gt;&gt; I'm

01:58:05.760 --> 01:58:09.590
proud to be here in my fathers name
presenting an award that carries

01:58:09.590 --> 01:58:13.199
forward the values of character and
activism that he lived.

01:58:14.330 --> 01:58:18.590
Stanford and the people of the business
school were dear to his heart and

01:58:18.590 --> 01:58:20.656
integral to his life for decades.

01:58:20.656 --> 01:58:24.688
&gt;From his early days as
an undergraduate in the 1930s,

01:58:24.688 --> 01:58:29.970
as an MBA student, and to the Dean in
the 1960s, and later as a trustee.

01:58:32.170 --> 01:58:34.270
Nominated and chosen by his or

01:58:34.270 --> 01:58:40.100
her peers, the recipient of the Ernest C
Arbuckle Award is the second year student,

01:58:40.100 --> 01:58:45.050
who by his or her active participation,
initiative, leadership, and

01:58:45.050 --> 01:58:49.510
personal integrity,
is judged as having contributed most

01:58:49.510 --> 01:58:53.310
to the fulfillment of the goals of
the Graduate School of Business in his or

01:58:53.310 --> 01:58:56.310
her actions,
both within school and society.

01:58:58.070 --> 01:59:02.660
Classmates described this year's recipient
with the following comments, and

01:59:02.660 --> 01:59:06.600
if you suspect who it is before
I finish reading the accolades,

01:59:06.600 --> 01:59:10.800
please let me continue so everyone can
hear why this student was nominated.

01:59:12.000 --> 01:59:16.070
This student, and I quote,
has been a pillar, perhaps the pillar,

01:59:16.070 --> 01:59:18.620
of the GSP community
over the past two years.

01:59:19.730 --> 01:59:24.130
The glue that brings both classes of
the GSB together through academic,

01:59:24.130 --> 01:59:26.570
social, and
community service related endeavors.

01:59:27.770 --> 01:59:29.500
This person is a natural leader,

01:59:29.500 --> 01:59:32.500
a positive personality
who befriended everyone.

01:59:34.650 --> 01:59:39.330
With an enthusiasm and spirit that
embodies the highest values of GSB,

01:59:39.330 --> 01:59:43.780
this student has worked to improve
the inclusiveness of our class.

01:59:43.780 --> 01:59:46.377
Another student said, unlike most of us,

01:59:46.377 --> 01:59:50.559
who get caught up in focusing on how
we can best achieve our own goals,

01:59:50.559 --> 01:59:54.473
this person's sole focus was on
improving the lives of others.

01:59:54.473 --> 01:59:58.737
There is so much more that this
person does behind the scenes,

01:59:58.737 --> 02:00:01.990
that makes the GSP a wonderful place.

02:00:01.990 --> 02:00:03.510
The impact if felt by all.

02:00:04.730 --> 02:00:08.250
An upstanding and respectful citizen,
in all interactions.

02:00:08.250 --> 02:00:11.970
This individual organized fellow
students to use their skills to

02:00:11.970 --> 02:00:13.534
help local small business'.

02:00:14.940 --> 02:00:19.260
This student has shown
an unparalleled enthusiasm to gather

02:00:19.260 --> 02:00:23.940
perspectives from all classmates
in order to put ideas into action.

02:00:27.220 --> 02:00:32.240
And better serve the broader community as
Co-President of the student association.

02:00:32.240 --> 02:00:35.830
He showed his relentless desire
to help both classmates and

02:00:35.830 --> 02:00:40.786
others by championing and creating the
Community Engagement Committee as well as

02:00:40.786 --> 02:00:43.176
the GSB Beyond the Bubble initiative.

02:00:43.176 --> 02:00:48.056
With much appreciation,
I present this award to Brian Solar.

02:00:48.056 --> 02:00:58.056
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

02:01:50.306 --> 02:01:52.239
&gt;&gt; The Alexander A Robicheaux Student

02:01:52.239 --> 02:01:55.203
Achievement Award in Finance
was established to honor

02:01:55.203 --> 02:01:59.651
Professor Robicheaux's outstanding
contribution to the teaching of finance at

02:01:59.651 --> 02:02:04.306
the Stanford Graduate School of Business
from 1960 until his death in 1978.

02:02:04.306 --> 02:02:08.300
The award is given to an MBA student
selected by the Finance Faculty for

02:02:08.300 --> 02:02:11.223
outstanding achievement
in the finance courses.

02:02:11.223 --> 02:02:14.432
The recipient receives the award and
also has his or

02:02:14.432 --> 02:02:16.973
her name engraved on a plaque at the GSP.

02:02:16.973 --> 02:02:20.181
This year's recipient of the Robicheaux
award is Peter Nurnberg.

02:02:20.181 --> 02:02:30.181
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

02:03:13.306 --> 02:03:15.081
&gt;&gt; Among the RJ MIllers Scholars,

02:03:15.081 --> 02:03:19.431
one student's academic achievement places
him or her at the top of the class.

02:03:19.431 --> 02:03:23.030
This student is designated as
the Henry Ford II, Scholar.

02:03:23.030 --> 02:03:28.750
The recipient's name is engraved on
a plaque on permanent display at the GSB.

02:03:28.750 --> 02:03:31.570
The student also receives
a substantial cash award.

02:03:34.000 --> 02:03:34.790
How substantial?

02:03:34.790 --> 02:03:36.580
We chose the biggest
number we could think of.

02:03:36.580 --> 02:03:37.970
One year's tuition at the GSB.

02:03:41.450 --> 02:03:44.640
I’m delighted that this year’s recipient
is someone who not only excelled in

02:03:44.640 --> 02:03:47.720
studies, but
also the contributed significantly to

02:03:47.720 --> 02:03:52.870
the broader intellectual environment at
GSB as a member of the academic committee.

02:03:52.870 --> 02:03:55.735
The 2015 Henry Ford Scholar
is Sagar Sanghvi.

02:03:55.735 --> 02:04:05.735
&gt;&gt; [APPLAUSE]

